/*
 * Every text the Kitsune app shows, in one file.
 *
 * How to edit:
 *   - Each line reads  "key" = "text";  Change only the text on the right.
 *   - The left side is the key the app looks up. Leave it exactly as it is,
 *     even after the text on the right has changed. A key that no longer
 *     matches makes the app show its original English text.
 *   - Keep every placeholder (%@, %d, %ld, %lu, %llu, %zu, %s, %.1f, %.2f,
 *     %.0f, %#lx) and keep them in the same order. %% is a percent sign.
 *   - \n is a line break; write \" for a double quote inside a text.
 *   - Spaces at the start or end of a text matter where the app joins it
 *     with a name or another text; keep them.
 *   - Texts used on several screens appear once, under Shared.
 *   - Plurals are made by the code: it adds "s" after "program" when the
 *     count is not 1.
 *   - After editing, check the file with:
 *       plutil -lint src/ios/en.lproj/Localizable.strings
 *
 * The app's name on the Home Screen is in InfoPlist.strings, next to this file.
 */

